+# TASK-260715-whtdsf — Rework 5 outcome
+
+Date: 2026-08-30 (Asia/Tbilisi)
+Base: `b3422b05226253a17676b9b84c764071fe3dbe74`
+
+## Result
+
+Ready for exact-artifact independent agent review. Rework 5 closes CR revision
+3 without retaining the false claim that repository default permissions cap a
+same-repository tag workflow or that a standard GitHub-hosted runner has no
+network access.
+
+- `release-prepare.yml` has one typed default-branch `repository_dispatch`
+  trigger. Tag/push, selectable-ref dispatch, and candidate-controlled upstream
+  workflow completion are not release entry points.
+- The request payload and sender are untrusted. The first job independently
+  validates the expected GitHub App installation, unique request ID, candidate
+  ancestry, trusted workflow/policy digests, and absent intended tag.
+- The short-lived external dispatch credential is truthfully inventoried with
+  the GitHub API-required `Contents: write` scope and no protected branch/tag
+  bypass. It cannot accept a candidate, approve an environment, obtain
+  production secrets, create the protected release tag, sign, or publish.
+- Protected publication creates the intended tag atomically at the accepted
+  commit. Policy fixtures reject every `push.tags` workflow trigger.
+- Pull-request public egress is explicit runner capability, not a deny claim.
+  PR authority remains credential-free/read-only with no protected environment,
+  privileged runner, private-production route, or promotable namespace.
+  Credential-bearing release jobs require enforceable job-specific egress
+  before secret access.
+- Trust invariant 4 now distinguishes inventoried read-only metadata access from
+  write elevation after protected-environment approval.
+
+Gate A0, iOS/TestFlight/App Store workflows, workflow implementation,
+production credentials, and a Linux-runner requirement for the macOS prototype
+remain out of scope. Human governance ratification remains independently
+tracked by `TASK-260717-2d308k`; it blocks publication, not downstream
+implementation after agent acceptance.
+
+## Artifacts and SHA-256
+
+- `docs/TASK-260715-whtdsf_ci-trust-and-quality-gate-contract.md` —
+  `41393dfb9e8f202d772e5d3d659ecab36117624f189ad8880c2f090317c41f36`
+- `diagrams/TASK-260715-whtdsf_ci-trust-boundary.puml` —
+  `b48705c50d466338ed9dffd9bdda201b59703bd8980a703f2414e92163f3b67b`
+- `diagrams/artefacts/TASK-260715-whtdsf_ci-trust-boundary.svg` —
+  `6386ca77f9bc389bf9c5595c63e879ba2b46ba35f1b567ac870e9e78fd0f7845`
+- `README.md` —
+  `5a6d83659443b8d6a5f5dfbd0fb61938b9df767267e48ddfc1637a15037adc98`
+- `LOGBOOK.md` —
+  `04c6ae145b5b8fb68abcdf110fe54e28671aba5f9d85bad6d66bd752d967f55c`
+
+## Validation and real exits
+
+- Required analysis status mutation: exit 0.
+- Tool readiness (`task-board`, `rg`, `git`, PlantUML 1.2026.6, `xmllint`,
+  `jq`): exit 0.
+- Official GitHub documentation reads for `repository_dispatch`, dispatch API
+  scope, permission calculation, hosted-runner networking, and reusable
+  workflow references: exit 0. Findings are stored in
+  `.temp/TASK-260715-whtdsf/research-github-release-request-rework5.md` and the
+  task-scoped provenance outcome.
+- Contract checker: exit 0; 26 six-field inventory rows, nine exact required
+  checks, 18 trace rows with one primary check, every required threat, and the
+  new trigger/token/network bounds are present; legacy tag-intake and
+  `workflow_run: completed` authority are absent.
+- All 27 referenced task IDs resolve on the authoritative board: exit 0.
+- PlantUML `-checkonly`, SVG render, SVG XML validation, PNG render, and manual
+  visual inspection: exit 0.
+- Tracked and untracked whitespace checks: corrected rerun exit 0. The first
+  probe exited 1 before checking artifacts because it used zsh's read-only
+  variable `status`; that command-construction failure is retained, not
+  misreported as an artifact failure.
+- Local authority and diagram-link readability: exit 0.
+- `task-board validate --json`: process exit 0 but content assertion exit 1,
+  `valid=false`, one `PARENT_STATUS_MISMATCH`: the Story is temporarily
+  `analysis` while its child aggregate is `to-review`. This is a lifecycle
+  state during the assigned analysis run; it must be rerun after reviewer and
+  producer handoff and is not reported green.
+- `scripts/tests/test-credential-free-validation.sh`: exit 1. It still expects
+  `ReluxProxyIOSUITests` and `ReluxProxyMacUITests`, while the accepted active
+  graph has six macOS-only schemes. `Project.swift`, this test, and
+  `scripts/check-workspace-schemes.sh` are unchanged by this candidate (exit
+  0). This is a pre-existing cross-owner regression, not reported green or
+  fixed.
+- Product Swift/Go builds were not rerun because this delta changes only the
+  binding documentation, focused diagram/render, README, logbook, and board
+  outcomes; it does not change product or workflow code.
+
+## Acceptance mapping
+
+1. Contract section 3 inventories every current, PR, authenticated request,
+   preparation, release, and deferred workflow trigger/job with trust/input,
+   permissions, environment/secrets, actual network capability/authorized use,
+   outputs/retention, and approval.
+2. Sections 2–3 make PR/fork jobs read-only, credential-free,
+   environment-free, and non-publishing without pretending public egress is
+   absent.
+3. Sections 4–5 bind nine checks and map all 18 requirements to exactly one
+   primary check plus macOS/iOS/relay/review ownership.
+4. Sections 7–8 cover fork, mutable action, cache, artifact, tag/workflow,
+   rerun, cancellation, concurrency, and credential threats with rejecting
+   fixtures at named production call sites.
+5. Section 9 records autonomous agent review and separately accountable human
+   ratification at `TASK-260717-2d308k`; no trust decision is silently disputed.
+
+## Board/decomposition audit and residual risk
+
+No board element or research task was created. The existing smallest atomic
+owner set covers every contract requirement; the obsolete bootstrap duplicate
+is closed with a self-verified gap/out-of-scope record. The four deferred iOS
+owners remain `blocked` with ADR-024/027 evidence, options, recommendation, and
+exact resume input. `references/negative-evidence.md` is absent after a readable
+repository/installed-skill path scan, so its contents remain unknown; the
+assignment's explicit rejecting-test rule is bound independently in section 8.
+
+Residual risks: workflow controls and their negative fixtures remain downstream
+implementation; human ratification blocks publication; exact egress-control
+technology for credentialed jobs is a policy-fill decision that must fail
+closed if unprovable; the pre-existing scheme-set test remains red.
