+The trusted-entry design follows GitHub's documented execution model:
+`repository_dispatch` loads a workflow that exists on the default branch and
+uses the default branch ref/SHA; its API requires a fine-grained caller with
+`Contents: write`; workflow/job YAML can adjust the repository's default token
+permissions; GitHub-hosted runners have public Internet access; and full commit
+SHAs are the safest reusable-workflow reference. See
+[events that trigger workflows](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/workflows-and-actions/events-that-trigger-workflows#repository_dispatch),
+[repository dispatch API](https://docs.github.com/en/rest/repos/repos#create-a-repository-dispatch-event),
